{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the structure well. Let me check the task12 raw session log to understand any additional context, and check the README.md and wiki dir for doc sync. But actually I mainly need to understand what to test.\n\nLet me check:\n1. The templates for `workflowScript`/`runs.run` occurrence\n2. The wiki directory\n3. The README.md for doc sync (mentions of O1/O2/O3 or related)\n4. Check what commands are registered (the 8 subcommands)\n5. Check bin/rick exists and works\n6. Check the `internal/` for redundant packages (executor, parser, actpath, logging, git, agent) - should be absent\n\nLet me also look at the loop readme-wiki-sync-loop referenced, and check the raw_session_test_gen.log for context (it might contain the previous test gen session).\n\nLet me run some checks.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_oEMVwz2Tb9X7A8GcmJ5t3187","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"===workflowScript/runs.run count in templates===\" && grep -roE 'workflowScript|runs\\.run|runs\\.all' internal/prompt/templates/ 2>/dev/null | wc -l && echo \"===files with workflowScript===\" && grep -rlE 'workflowScript|runs\\.run' internal/prompt/templates/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"===internal redundant dirs (should be absent)===\" && for d in executor parser actpath logging git agent; do if [ -d \"internal/$d\" ]; then echo \"EXISTS internal/$d\"; else echo \"absent internal/$d\"; fi; done && echo \"===5 dirs check===\" && for d in cmd handler env builder runtime; do if [ -d \"internal/$d\" ]; then echo \"OK internal/$d\"; else echo \"MISSING internal/$d\"; fi; done"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_LLbIq4ujHNHCCx6LRX134219","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && echo \"===bin/rick===\" && ls -la bin/ && echo \"===rick --help===\" && ./bin/rick --help 2>&1 | head -40; echo \