\", the agents should already be deployed to `~/.rick/pi/agent/`.\n\nHmm, but they're not deployed currently. So either:\n1. The test should fail (correct RED — agents not deployed yet, init-pi needs re-run)\n2. Or I should deploy to a temp dir as part of the test.\n\nLet me think about what's the most faithful interpretation of the 测试方法.\n\nThe 测试方法 says: \"操作 = 依次执行 KR1 的三组断言\". KR1 O3 = \"workflowScript 计数 ≥1 + 3 个 agent 文件 + rick-gates helper.py\".\n\nThe most natural reading: check that the 3 agent files exist (at the deployed location), and rick-gates helper.py exists.\n\nBut there's ambiguity about the location. Let me check what a reasonable test would do.\n\nActually, I realize I should look at how the previous test scripts (task8, task9, task10, task11) handled similar checks, especially task9 which was about agents. Let me check task9.py's agent check logic.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_ueZES11KXq9x6oTZf7lk1637","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task9.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":2634,"output":3234,"cacheRead":52224,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":3161,"totalTokens":58092,"cost":{"input":0.00114579,"output":0.00281358,"cacheRead":0.00018931200000000002,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.004148682}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915974706,"responseId":"6a625278-6ef2-4891-b50a-06cd9d142535","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"}}
