g task11's regex).\n\nNow let me also think about the boundary test (command --help). The 8 subcommands are: plan, doing, easy, learning, dream, tools, human-loop, ctrl.\n\nWait, let me verify the exact subcommands. From `./bin/rick --help`:\n```\nAvailable Commands:\n  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell\n  ctrl        Monitor and intervene in a background doing session\n  doing       Execute tasks in a job\n  dream       Cross-job global reflection and skill evolution\n  easy        Start an interactive easy AI coding session\n  help        Help about any command\n  human-loop  Start a human-loop thinking session with AI assistance\n  learning    Analyze and document learnings from job execution\n  plan        Plan a new job with AI assistance\n  tools       Meta-skill tools for validating and managing Rick workflows\n```\n\nThe 8 subcommands to test: plan, doing, easy, learning, dream, tools, human-loop, ctrl. (completion and help are excluded — they're auto-generated by cobra).\n\nSo I'll test: `./bin/rick <cmd> --help` for each of the 8, plus `./bin/rick --help`.\n\nFor \"无 panic\", I check exit code 0 and that stderr/stdout doesn't contain \"panic\".\n\nFor \"含 plan/doing/easy/learning/dream/tools/human-loop/ctrl\", I check the root --help output contains these command names.\n\nNow the rollback test (异常/回滚兜底):\n```\ngit log --oneline -1  → record current release commit\ngit worktree add /tmp/rick-rollback <release-commit>\ncd /tmp/rick-rollback && ./scripts/build.sh && ./bin/rick --help (exit 0)\n```\n\nThis is a potentially expensive test (build.sh compiles the Go project). But it's required by the test method.\n\nAlso: \"不污染主工作区；`.rick/domain/` 无本 task 变更\" — check `git status .rick/domain/` has no changes.\n\nLet me check the scripts/build.sh to understand what it does.\n\nActually, let me check build.sh and verify the rollback test works.\n\nLet me also think about whether the rollback test is appropriate to include. The