{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"There are many uncommitted changes in the working tree. The `.rick/domain/project-conventions.md` modification is from a previous task (job_28 lesson), not task12. The task12 test's rollback check \"`.rick/domain/` 无本 task 变更\" means the test should verify that the test script itself (and task12) doesn't introduce `.rick/domain/` changes. But actually, since there's already a pre-existing modification, the test can't simply assert `git status .rick/domain/` is empty.\n\nHmm. Let me think about this. The rollback test's expected result is \"可回滚且 rick 仍可编译运行（不污染主工作区；`.rick/domain/` 无本 task 变更）\".\n\nThis is about the test script's own rollback verification not polluting the main workspace. The `git worktree add` creates a separate worktree, so it doesn't pollute the main workspace. And \".rick/domain/ 无本 task 变更\" means task12 (this test task) shouldn't introduce changes to `.rick/domain/`.\n\nSince the test script is just a test (it doesn't modify `.rick/domain/`), this is inherently satisfied. But the test can verify:\n1. After the rollback verification, the main workspace's git status for `.rick/domain/` is unchanged (i.e., the rollback worktree operation didn't add new changes to `.rick/domain/`).\n\nActually, a cleaner approach: record `git status --porcelain .rick/domain/` before the rollback test, run the rollback test, then record it after, and assert they're identical (the rollback didn't introduce new `.rick/domain/` changes).\n\nBut actually, the simplest and most faithful interpretation: the rollback test should verify:\n1. Record current commit\n2. Create worktree at that commit\n3. Build + run --help (exit 0)\n4. Clean up worktree\n5. Verify main workspace not polluted (the worktree operation doesn't change main workspace's `.rick/domain/`)\n\nFor \"不污染主工作区\", the key check is that `git worktree add` + `git worktree remove` doesn't leave the main workspace in a different state. Since the test runs in the main repo but the worktree is in /tmp, the main workspace isn't touched.\n\nI think the cleanest implementation:\n1. Before: snapshot `git status --porcelain` (or at least `.rick/domain/` status)\n2. Get HEAD commit\n3. `git worktree add --detach <tmpdir> HEAD`\n4. Build in worktree: `./scripts/build.sh`\n5. Run `./bin/rick --help` in worktree → exit 0\n6. `git worktree remove <tmpdir>`\n7. After: snapshot `git status --porcelain .rick/domain/` → assert unchanged (no new .rick/domain changes)\n\nActually, the `.rick/domain/ 无本 task 变更` check — the test script itself should not modify `.rick/domain/`. So I can snapshot before and after and compare.\n\nLet me think about what's most valuable and faithful. The test method's 异常 path expected: \"可回滚且 rick 仍可编译运行（不污染主工作区；`.rick/domain/` 无本 task 变更）\".\n\nSo the assertions for the rollback test:\n1. Rollback worktree builds successfully (build.sh exit 0)\n2. Rollback worktree `./bin/rick --help` exit 0 (rick still compiles/runs)\n3. Main workspace not polluted (`.rick/domain/` has no changes introduced by this test)\n\nFor #3, I'll snapshot `.rick/domain/` git status before and after the rollback operation and assert equal.\n\nNow, let me also consider: the build in the worktree will build from the committed source at HEAD. But the worktree has uncommitted changes NOT included (since worktree add uses HEAD commit). So the build will be of the committed state, which should be task11's committed state. That's fine — the rollback test verifies the committed state is buildable.\n\nActually, wait — there's a subtlety. The worktree at HEAD (be847c7) will have the committed source. The `internal/` directory, templates, etc. are all committed (they show as clean in git status, except the .rick/ files and .rick/dream/prompts). Let me verify that internal/ and the templates are committed.\n\nActually, from `git status --porcelain`, I see no `internal/` files listed as modified/untracked, so internal/ is fully committed. Good. The templates (internal/prompt/templates/) are committed.\n\nBut wait — are the templates committed? Let me verify. The task11 commit (be847c7) should include the migrated templates. Let me check that `git status` doesn't show internal/prompt/templates/ as modified. From the status output, no internal/ files are modified. So yes, templates are committed.\n\nOK. Now, one concern: the worktree build might take a while (Go compile). But it should be fine within a reasonable timeout. Let me set a generous timeout (e.g., 600s for the build).\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether the rollback test should be included in full. It's in the 测试方法, so yes. But I should make it robust and not too slow.\n\nLet me now also verify the exact O2 \"职责与 spec 对应\" and whether I need to check it. The 测试方法's O2 says \"5 目录存在 + 6 冗余包 test ! -d\". So just those two checks. The \"职责与 spec 对应\" is part of the O2 description but the 测试方法 reduces it to directory existence. I'll stick to the 测试方法's explicit checks.\n\nBut wait, KR5 (扩展点验收) is in the plan's 关键结果 but NOT in the 测试方法. Should I include it? The test prompt says \"根据上面的'测试方法'实现每个测试步骤\". The 测试方法 has 3 paths. So I'll implement those 3 paths. KR5 (extension seam) and KR4 (README/wiki sync) are not in the 测试方法, so I'll focus on the 3 test paths.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The test prompt says \"你需要根据任务的测试方法生成一个 Python 测试脚本\" and \"实现测试方法中的所有步骤\". The 测试方法 section has 3 paths. So I implement those 3.\n\nBut there's also the \"测试质量自检\" which says I must run the test and judge. And the \"Cialdini 合规原则\" says \"测试脚本生成必须覆盖全部验收条件，不得遗漏任何测试步骤.\"\n\nHmm, \"覆盖全部验收条件\" — the acceptance criteria are the three O + README/wiki sync. The 测试方法 covers the three O (via 正常路径) + command availability (边界) + rollback (异常). The README/wiki sync is part of the task goal but its testing isn't in the 测试方法's explicit steps.\n\nWait, let me re-read the task goal and the 测试方法 more carefully. The task goal includes \"