{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"All 8 subcommands exit 0. The workflowScript file count is 8 (≥1), runs.run in 14 files.\n\nNow I have everything I need. Let me write the test script.\n\nSummary of what I'll test:\n\n**Test 1 (正常路径 - 三 O 验收):**\n\nO1 (spec 信息内核):\n- `.rick/domain/spec.md` exists\n- `.rick/domain/rick-spec.md` exists\n- Both contain 四要素 keywords: 模块边界, 职责, 接口契约, 验收标准\n- rick-spec.md contains '功能等价'\n- spec.md contains operational criteria (dry-run / go test / 集成测试)\n\nO2 (三层金字塔 + 做薄):\n- 5 directories exist: internal/cmd, internal/handler, internal/env, internal/builder, internal/runtime\n- 6 redundant packages deleted: executor, parser, actpath, logging, git, agent (test ! -d)\n\nO3 (pibuilder pi 对齐):\n- workflowScript count ≥1 (in templates)\n- 3 agent files (think/research/exporter) deployed to temp RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR via real DeployRickCustomizations\n- rick-gates extension deployed (extensions/rick-gates/helper.py)\n- `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` source exists\n- natural language trigger count decreased (< baseline)\n\n**Test 2 (边界 - 命令全可用):**\n- `./bin/rick --help` exit 0, no panic, contains 8 subcommand names\n- 8 subcommands `--help` each exit 0, no panic\n\n**Test 3 (异常 - 回滚兜底):**\n- Record HEAD commit\n- git worktree add to temp dir\n- build.sh + --help exit 0 in worktree\n- cleanup worktree\n- `.rick/domain/` no changes introduced (snapshot before/after)\n\nNow, for the O3 agent deployment, I'll use the same pattern as task9.py: a temp Go program that calls `env.DeployRickCustomizations()` with RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR set to a temp dir.\n\nActually, wait — should I use the temp Go program approach, or just check `~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/`? \n\nLet me reconsider. The test method's O3 says \"3 个 agent 文件\". The KR1 detail says deploy to temp RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR and check. The task9.py pattern is proven. I'll use the temp Go program approach for the agent deployment check, because:\n1. It verifies REAL deployment behavior\n2. It's self-contained (doesn't depend on init-pi having been run)\n3. It matches KR1's \"显式 export RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR=<temp> 后 ... 3 文件存在 + extensions/rick-gates/ 已部署\"\n\nBut actually, there's a subtlety. The temp Go program imports `github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/env`. This requires the temp program to be INSIDE the module (internal package import restriction). task9.py handles this by creating a `.tmp_task9_deploy_*` directory inside the repo root.\n\nI'll replicate this. But actually, I want to keep it simpler. Let me think about whether I can just use `go run` with a temp dir inside the repo.\n\nActually, task9.py's approach is well-tested. Let me reuse it but simplify since I only need the \"正常路径\" (deploy + check 3 files + rick-gates extension), not the full boundary/exception coverage (task9 already covered those).\n\nActually, let me reconsider the whole thing. For task12, the O3 check is an end-to-end acceptance, not a unit test. The simplest faithful check:\n\nOption A: Check `~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/{think,research,exporter}.md` + `~/.rick/pi/agent/extensions/rick-gates/helper.py` (default deployment location). This requires init-pi to have been run. Currently NOT deployed → test would FAIL.\n\nOption B: Deploy to temp dir via temp Go program, check files. Self-contained, always works if the deploy code works.\n\nOption C: Check BOTH the source (`.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` + templates/skills/{think,research,exporter}.md embedded) AND do a real deploy to temp.\n\nThe test method KR1 says \"显式 export RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR=<temp>（或改用 ~/.rick/pi/agent 默认路径）后，$RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/agents/{think,research,exporter}.md 3 文件存在 + $RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR/extensions/rick-gates/ 已部署\".\n\nThis clearly means: set RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR to temp (or use default), then the files should exist (after deploy). The phrase \"已部署\" (deployed) implies an active deploy step.\n\nI'll go with Option B (temp dir deploy via temp Go program), which is the most faithful to KR1 and self-contained.\n\nActually, wait. Let me reconsider once more. There's a simpler interpretation: the test just checks the DEFAULT location `~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/`. The prerequisite \"`rick tools init-pi` 已成功\" means the deploy already happened. So the test checks the CURRENT state at the default location.\n\nBut this is fragile: if init-pi hasn't been run, the test fails for an environmental reason, not a code reason. And it would pollute the real `~/.rick/pi/agent`.\n\nGiven task9.py established the temp-dir pattern and it's cleaner, I'll use the temp-dir deploy approach. This is the \"real behavior, not mock\" approach (per testing-anti-patterns).\n\nLet me write the test script now.\n\nFor the temp Go program, I need to handle the deploy. Let me write it carefully.\n\nThe deploy program:\n```go\npackage main\n\nimport (\n    \"fmt\"\n    \"os\"\n    \"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/env\"\n)\n\nfunc main() {\n    target := \".\"\n    if len(os.Args) > 1 {\n        target = os.Args[1]\n    }\n    if err := os.Chdir(target); err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chdir %s failed: %v\\n\", target, err)\n        os.Exit(2)\n    }\n    if err := env.DeployRickCustomizations(); err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"deploy failed: %v\\n\", err)\n        os.Exit(1)\n    }\n    fmt.Println(\"deploy-ok\")\n}\n```\n\nThis is identical to task9's. I'll reuse it.\n\nThe deploy requires `workspace.GetRickDir()` to locate the `.rick/skills` source. Let me check how GetRickDir works — it probably locates the repo root via go.mod or .rick marker.\n\nActually, task9.py's approach: run the Go program with cwd = repo_root, and the program does `os.Chdir(target)` where target = repo_root. Then `workspace.GetRickDir()` finds the `.rick` dir.\n\nLet me check GetRickDir to be sure it works from repo root."}}
