{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There's a PermissionError when trying to remove the home dirs. The dirs are `drwx------` (0700) owned by `hadoop-recsys`, but the content includes `go/pkg/mod/golang.org/toolchain@.../bin/go` which is likely read-only (Go toolchain files are extracted with read-only permissions, mode 0555 or 0444). Actually, rmtree should handle read-only files by chmod'ing them... actually no, `shutil.rmtree` does NOT chmod read-only files on some systems. Actually, `shutil.rmtree` has an `onerror` handler. By default, if a file is read-only, `os.unlink` fails with PermissionError on some filesystems.\n\nWait, actually, the PermissionError is likely because the Go toolchain files are extracted with read-only permissions (0444/0555), and `shutil.rmtree` tries to unlink them but can't because the PARENT directory doesn't have write permission... no, the parent dir is `drwx------` (0700) owned by the user.\n\nActually, the classic issue: `go run` downloads the toolchain and extracts it with read-only permissions. `shutil.rmtree` on a read-only file fails because it uses `os.unlink` without first making the file writable. The standard fix is `shutil.rmtree(path, onerror=lambda func, path, exc: (os.chmod(path, stat.S_IWRITE), func(path)))`.\n\nBut wait — why is this a problem at all? Because I set `HOME=home` in the deploy env, which causes Go to download the toolchain to `$HOME/go/pkg/mod`. This is an unintended side effect.\n\nThe real fix: DON'T set HOME to a temp dir. The task9.py set HOME to avoid polluting the real home, but the deploy program (env.DeployRickCustomizations) doesn't actually use HOME for anything except... let me check. Does DeployRickCustomizations use HOME?\n\nLooking at the deploy chain:\n- `workspace.GetRickDir()` → uses `os.Getwd()` (cwd), NOT HOME.\n- `runtime.AgentDir()` → uses `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR` env or `os.UserHomeDir()` (which on Linux reads `$HOME`).\n\nSo HOME matters for `os.UserHomeDir()`, but I'm setting `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR` explicitly, so `AgentDir()` returns the RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR value directly (the HOME fallback is never hit). So I actually DON'T need to set HOME at all!\n\nBut wait, `os.UserHomeDir()` in Go reads `$HOME` on Linux. Since I set `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR`, AgentDir() returns that without calling UserHomeDir. So HOME is only needed if RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR is empty.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: setting HOME to a temp dir causes `go run` to re-download the toolchain/module cache to `$HOME/go`, which is the cause of the large read-only temp dirs.\n\nThe fix: Don't override HOME. Keep the real HOME so Go uses the existing module cache. Only set RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR to the temp dir.\n\nActually, but task9.py set HOME to avoid the deploy touching real `~/.rick`. But since we set RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR, the deploy writes to the temp agent_dir, not `~/.rick/pi/agent`. So HOME doesn't matter for the deploy output.\n\nHowever, there's another subtlety: does `go run` with the real HOME cause any issue? No — it just uses the existing module cache (~/go/pkg/mod), which is faster and doesn't create temp dirs.\n\nSo the fix is: remove the `env['HOME'] = home` line and the `home` temp dir entirely. Just set `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR` and keep HOME as-is.\n\nWait, but let me double-check: does `os.UserHomeDir()` in Go return the real home even when HOME is unset? It reads `$HOME`. If I don't override HOME, it's the real `/home/hadoop-recsys`. And `AgentDir()` with RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR set returns the temp dir directly. So the deploy writes to temp agent_dir. \n\nBut actually, wait — there's still a subtle issue. Even without overriding HOME, if I DON'T set RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR, the deploy would write to `~/.rick/pi/agent`. But I DO set RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR, so it writes to temp. Good.\n\nSo the fix: remove HOME override, keep only RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR.\n\nLet me also clean up the existing leftover temp dirs. The read-only files need special handling. Let me use `shutil.rmtree` with an onerror handler that chmods.\n\nActually, I should also fix my cleanup code to be robust against read-only files (in case there's a similar issue). But if I remove the HOME override, the go run won't create the go/pkg/mod dirs, so cleanup will be trivial.\n\nLet me update the test script:\n1. Remove `home = tempfile.mkdtemp(...)` and `env['HOME'] = home` and `shutil.rmtree(home)`.\n\nLet me make this edit.\n\nAlso, let me clean up the leftover temp dirs using a chmod-based rmtree.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"The `HOME` override causes Go to re-download its toolchain into read-only temp dirs. Since I already set `RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR`, I don't need to override `HOME` at all. Let me fix that and clean up the leftovers."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_A6KFbLhMzurXwvopd0si5618","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task12.py","edits":[{"oldText":"    # think/research/exporter 落盘为 pi agent（真实 deploy，隔离 RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR）\n    agent_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task12_agent_')\n    home = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task12_home_')\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env['RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR'] = agent_dir\n    env['HOME'] = home\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'run', '.', REPO_ROOT], cwd=prog_dir, timeout=240, env=env)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations exit=%d: %s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('pi agent %s.md 未落盘: %s' % (name, p))\n        gate_deployed = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'extensions', 'rick-gates', 'helper.py')\n        if not os.path.isfile(gate_deployed):\n            errors.append('rick-gates 扩展未部署: %s' % gate_deployed)\n    shutil.rmtree(agent_dir, ignore_errors=True)\n    shutil.rmtree(home, ignore_errors=True)","newText":"    # think/research/exporter 落盘为 pi agent（真实 deploy，隔离 RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR）。\n    # 只覆盖 RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR，不覆盖 HOME（避免 go run 把工具链重新下载到临时\n    # 目录形成只读 go/pkg/mod，导致清理失败）；AgentDir() 优先读 RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR。\n    agent_dir = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix='rick_task12_agent_')\n    env = os.environ.copy()\n    env['RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR'] = agent_dir\n    rc, out, err = run([go, 'run', '.', REPO_ROOT], cwd=prog_dir, timeout=240, env=env)\n    if rc != 0:\n        errors.append('DeployRickCustomizations exit=%d: %s' % (rc, tail(err or out)))\n    else:\n        for name in AGENTS:\n            p = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'agents', name + '.md')\n            if not os.path.isfile(p):\n                errors.append('pi agent %s.md 未落盘: %s' % (name, p))\n        gate_deployed = os.path.join(agent_dir, 'extensions', 'rick-gates', 'helper.py')\n        if not os.path.isfile(gate_deployed):\n            errors.append('rick-gates 扩展未部署: %s' % gate_deployed)\n    shutil.rmtree(agent_dir, ignore_errors=True)"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":129,"output":2021,"cacheRead":87424,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1176,"totalTokens":89574,"cost":{"input":0.000056115,"output":0.0017582700000000001,"cacheRead":0.00031691200000000003,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0021312970000000003}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786916319887,"responseId":"227e6684-9702-4f75-b379-3bd4fc88ed63","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_A6KFbLhMzurXwvopd0si5618","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 1 block(s) in /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/.rick/jobs/job_35/doing/tests/task12.py."}],"details":{"diff":"     ...\n 261         current = total_matches(TRIGGER_RE, templates)\n 262         if current >= baseline:\n 263             errors.append('自然语言触发词计数未下降：当前 %d >= 基线 %d' % (current, baseline))\n 264 \n-265     # think/research/exporter 落盘为 pi agent（真实 deploy，隔离 RICK_PI_AGENT_DIR）\n+265   